  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_006 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieves 0.535 acc, outperforming config_014 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) at 0.485 acc, confirming that adding the image modality with concat fusion provides a meaningful ~5% boost. Uncertainty: We have no evidence yet on whether multiprofile with aggregation improves over singleprofile. Question tested: config_024 is the minimal extension of config_006—same model setting, same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), same image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), same fusion (concat)—but switches to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation. This isolates the effect of multiprofile + simple averaging without confounding changes to encoders or fusion. Why best: It directly extends the current best configuration with the smallest possible change, making the result easy to attribute to the profile/aggregation decision. If it improves, we gain confidence that multiprofile is worth pursuing and can then test transformer aggregation or other encoders; if it does not, we avoid wasting budget on more complex multiprofile variants."
}

